Types of Xpath:-
---------------

1) Absolute xpath (full xpath) - Absolute xpath traverse through each node till it finds element.

Ex: /html/body/header/div/div/div/div[2]/div/input

2) Relative xpath (partial xpath) - Relative xpath directly jump and find the element by using attribute.

Ex: //*[@id="search"]/input

Difference between Absolute & Relative xpaths?

Absolute xpath starts with /  ---> represents root node
Relative xpath starts with //

Absolute xpath do not use attributes
Relative xpath works with attribute

Absolute xpath traverse through each node till it finds element
Relative xpath directly jump and find the element by using attribute

